# Optional per-developer overrides. Copy to backend/.env (git-ignored) only if you need one.
# Never commit backend/.env or .env.local — they contain database passwords.
#
# Where the database settings normally come from:
#   - Nothing set            -> local SQLite file (backend/instance/lifeos.db). No Neon access needed.
#   - <project>/.env.local   -> written by `neon env pull` / `neon checkout` for team members
#                               with Neon access. See README > "Database".
# A value in backend/.env takes priority over .env.local.

# Neon Postgres connection string (pooled), e.g. from the Neon console > Connect.
# Paste it as shown (postgresql://...); the app adds the driver name itself.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Direct (unpooled) connection, used only to create tables at startup.
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# Only needed in production; development generates one in instance/secret_key.
# SECRET_KEY=
